            summary: "One hairline that separates rows inside a single container: table and list rows, the rule under a tab rail, the edge between two columns of one panel. It draws `border.hairline` in `color.border.hairline` and nothing else. Everywhere else in Prism the luminance ladder and the spacing scale do the separating, so a Divider is the exception, not the default.",
