            implemented: [],
            platformNotes: [("ios", "full — `screen` and both forms of `sheet`. A phone never reaches the desktop width, so a host never asks it for `drawer`, and a `drawer` requested anyway renders as a `sheet`."), ("ipados", "full — all three presentations; a host asks for `drawer` at desktop width, which every iPad reaches in landscape, and for `sheet` below it."), ("macos", "adapted — Sheet's macOS form has no drag and no detents, so a `sheet` with no stage renders as `drawer`, a `sheet` over a stage renders as `screen`, and `detents` is ignored; Escape dismisses a drawer while focus is inside it. Compact density tightens the padding and the row height."), ("watchos", "adapted — `presentation: screen` only, with no stage, no readout, no glass, no Sheet and no drawer (ADR-0010 Tier 3; Sheet, Toolbar, ChartContainer, HeroNumber, Skeleton and EmptyState are all `watchos: none`). The screen is the title, one hero and a vertical stack of at most three ListRows on the page: the hero is a StatTile at `size: lg`, whose value renders at the watch's type.metric.xl of 40 px (ADR-0021 §2 as amended by ADR-0030 §7). There is no action bar - the actions become rows - `loading` dims the rows instead of drawing a Skeleton, and `error` is one row with the message."), ("web-desktop", "adapted — as macOS, because Sheet's web-desktop form is the same edge drawer: a `sheet` with no stage renders as `drawer`, a `sheet` over a stage as `screen`, Escape dismisses a drawer while focus is inside it, and `detents` is ignored.")],
